eginDt": "06/22/2026", "sessionEndDt": "08/04/2026", "sessionLong": "Six Week Summer", "exploreCriteriaIds": []}], "description": "This course is designed to introduce students to ideas and concepts that help explain the multi-faceted forces that shape cities, their growth and urban life within them, and urban inequality. The course will use a workshop format that includes brief lectures, readings (or other formats such as audiovisual material or art) and discussions, and a sequence of exercises to learn the basic methods and collaborative processes used in urban studies and planning. Students will not just learn about issues related to urban sustainability and justice; they will also explore ways to engage and act to build more just, sustainable, and healthier cities for everyone. During the last week of the class, students will also learn from special guests working collaboratively with communities. Grades will be based on the overall performance of student presentations and participation.", "catalogBreadth": null, "catalogDistr": null, "catalogEnrollmentPriority": "Enrollment limited to: non-URS students, high school students in 11 and 12 grades, and anyone with a minimum of a high school diploma interested in exploring cities and urban environments.", "catalogLang": null, "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": null, "catalogAttribute": null, "catalogWhenOffered": null, "catalogComments": null, "catalogPrereqCoreq": null, "catalogPrereq": "", "catalogCoreq": "", "catalogFee": null, "catalogSatisfiesReq": null, "catalogPermission": null, "catalogCourseSubfield": null, "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "AR", "catalogName": null, "catalogNextOffered": null, "lastTermsOffered": "2026SU, 2025SU, 2024SU", "catalogCredits": null, "catalogGradeOption": null, "catalogLocation": null, "catalogCrosslisted": null, "catalogCrosslistings": null, "catalogComeets": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": []}, {"strm": 2930, "crseId": 373896, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "CRP",